cription":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-03-04T18:41:38Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T23:34:12Z","closed_at":"2025-03-04T21:44:18Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.4.stable.official [4c311cbee]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1080 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7242) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-4790K CPU @ 4.00GHz (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThis bug or non functional feature issue has been mentioned under issue \"#101984\", but for a different version. \n\nThe settings I'm using: \"always on top\" is checked in the project display/window settings with advanced settings checked and run my game with \"Embed Game on Next Play\" checked and \"Make Game Workspace Floating on Next Play\" unchecked. \n\nThe floating workspace window will not obey the always on top setting which i find a little annoying, I would like to be able to use the workspace as a floating window and not have it go under when i click out of it, mostly so i can see the output prints as the game runs and if i adjust the output dock's size.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCheck the setting \"advanced settings\" and under display/window, check \"always on top\", and on the new 4.4 game tab, check \"Embed Game on Next Play\" and uncheck \"Make Game Workspace Floating on Next Play\".\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nWill work on any project as far as i can tell.","closed_by":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravata